item.description:
20-250 GBP | Wix mobile optimisation and website tidy-up – mediation.ltd

I’m looking for an experienced Wix freelancer to help polish and optimise mediation.ltd, with the mobile experience as the main priority.

The website is already live and works well on desktop. The branding, structure, design direction and copy are established, so this is not a redesign or copywriting project. I need someone who can take the existing desktop design and translate it into a cleaner, simpler and more deliberately designed mobile experience.

The finished mobile site should still feel unmistakably like mediation.ltd, but it should be easier to read, navigate and interact with on a phone.

Scope of work

1. Mobile optimisation

Please review the site page by page in Wix, starting with the homepage and the principal user journeys.

I’d like particular attention paid to:

inconsistent or excessive spacing;
margins and padding;
typography and heading sizes;
awkward line breaks or text wrapping;
elements that feel cramped or oversized;
alignment of text and visual elements;
buttons and calls to action;
sections that become unnecessarily long when stacked on mobile;
mobile navigation;
header and footer presentation; and
overall visual hierarchy.

I don't want the desktop layout simply squeezed onto a smaller screen. Where necessary, I’m happy for elements to be reordered, resized or presented differently on mobile, provided the existing copy, brand and overall site structure are retained.

2. Responsive treatment of key content

The site contains several content-led sections, including Why Gregory Hunt?, Is mediation the right next step?, Gregory's approach and A mediator lawyers can recommend with confidence. These need to retain their impact and hierarchy when viewed on a smaller screen.

Please consider whether cards, columns, feature blocks and other desktop elements need a cleaner mobile treatment rather than simply being stacked.

3. Navigation and calls to action

Please review:

mobile menus;
navigation between pages and sections;
button positioning and sizing;
tap targets;
email and telephone links;
calls to action;
footer links; and
links between mediation.ltd and HuntADR.com.

The goal is to make it very easy for someone arriving on a phone to understand the proposition, explore Gregory's approach and discuss a mediation without unnecessary friction.

4. Forms and functionality

Please thoroughly test any forms and interactive elements on mobile as part of the work.

This should include:

form layout;
field sizing and spacing;
required fields and validation;
buttons;
error and confirmation behaviour; and
successful submission from a mobile device.

5. Basic on-page SEO

While working in Wix, please review the fundamentals rather than undertaking a wider SEO project:

sensible H1/H2/H3 hierarchy;
page titles;
meta descriptions;
image alt text;
internal linking;
image sizing/optimisation; and
any obvious broken links or SEO issues.

Please flag any recommendation involving a change to an existing URL or site structure before implementing it.

6. Desktop protection

The existing desktop presentation should remain intact.

After making mobile changes, please check the desktop and tablet versions to ensure that responsive changes haven't inadvertently affected layouts, styling or functionality elsewhere.

Brand and content

Please work within the existing mediation.ltd visual identity.

I’m looking for refinement and consistency rather than a new design direction. Please don't independently rewrite the copy, change the positioning or substantially restructure the site.

If you spot something that you believe could be implemented better, I'm very happy for you to recommend it before making the change.

Technical safeguards

The site has previously been through domain/DNS configuration work, so this brief does not include changes to:

domain settings;
DNS or nameservers;
SSL configuration;
MX/email records; or
other domain-level settings.

Please check with me before making any significant technical, structural or URL changes.

Working approach

I'd prefer the work to be undertaken incrementally rather than through a large number of simultaneous live changes.

Ideally:

Review the current site and flag any significant issues.
Start with the homepage/mobile framework.
Establish a consistent mobile treatment for typography, spacing, buttons and content blocks.
Apply that consistently across the remaining pages.
Test navigation, links, forms and calls to action.
Complete a final desktop, tablet and mobile QA check.

I'd like to review the work on several mobile devices before the project is considered complete.

What success looks like

At the end of the project, mediation.ltd should:

feel intentionally designed for mobile rather than adapted from desktop;
retain the established brand and professional character;
have clear, consistent spacing and typography;
be easy to scan and read;
have an obvious visual hierarchy;
make navigation and calls to action easy to use;
work properly across common mobile screen sizes;
contain no obvious overlapping, wrapping or alignment issues;
have functioning forms and links; and
remain strong and consistent on desktop.
Experience required

Please provide examples of Wix websites you have personally worked on, ideally where you were responsible for mobile/responsive optimisation.

I'm particularly interested in someone with:

strong Wix experience;
demonstrable mobile/responsive design skills;
an excellent eye for spacing, typography and visual consistency;
experience troubleshooting Wix layouts;
experience with forms and mobile usability;
a working knowledge of on-page SEO; and
the ability to improve an existing design without unnecessarily redesigning it.

Please also confirm your hourly or project rate, availability and estimated timescale.

There may be an opportunity for ongoing ad-hoc Wix support after this initial project.
